# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Model weights
# Regenerate with train_cte.py, or attach to a GitHub release.
# Never commit these: they are tens to hundreds of MB and bloat history permanently.
*.pth
*.pt
*.h5
*.ckpt

# Exception: the safety-case perception model is only ~1.5 MB. Commit it, so the
# whole PRISM/guard/shift pipeline is reproducible without retraining or access
# to the simulator. (The coursework checkpoints were 80-110 MB each - those are
# the ones this rule exists to keep out.)
!results_cte/cte_model.pth

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Collected data
# Frames + cte_log.csv from collect_cte_data.py. Thousands of JPGs per track.
# Regenerate by re-running collection against the simulator.
data_cte/
data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Large artefacts
*.mp4
*.avi
*.npy
*.npz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Results
# results_cte/ is committed by default because the small JSON/CSV/PRISM files
# ARE the evidence base for the report. Only bulk artefacts are excluded above.
# If a specific run folder is scratch, add it explicitly here, e.g.:
# results_cte/scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Tooling
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
!results_cte/**/*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- OS
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store